# [[.Title]]

[[.Title]] is a Go web app built on [C4Stack](https://github.com/coolapso/c4stack):
Gin, Templ, HTMX and PostgreSQL, with [[if .Hanko]]Hanko for sign-in[[else]]sign-in by email code or passkey[[end]].

## Run it locally

You need Go, [Task](https://taskfile.dev) 3.53.1 or later, Docker and OpenSSL.
`Taskfile.yml` holds the development settings, and makes a new secret key each time a
task starts; there is no settings file to fill in.

[[if .Hanko -]]
1. Create a [Hanko Cloud](https://cloud.hanko.io) project with `http://localhost:8080`
   as its app URL, and put its API URL in `Taskfile.yml` as
   `[[.EnvPrefix]]_HANKO_API_URL`.
2. Start the database and apply migrations:

   ```sh
   task db:up db:migrate
   ```
3. Start the app with live reload, then open http://localhost:8080:

   ```sh
   task dev
   ```
[[- else -]]
1. Start the database and Mailpit, and apply migrations:

   ```sh
   task db:up mail:up db:migrate
   ```
2. Start the app with live reload, then open http://localhost:8080:

   ```sh
   task dev
   ```
3. Sign in with any address. The code arrives in Mailpit, at http://localhost:8025.
[[- end]]

`task --list` shows every task. `go run . help` shows the app's commands.

To add pages, tables, API keys, credits and more, follow the
[C4Stack guide]([[.Docs]]/guide.md).

## Where things are

| Path | What it holds |
|---|---|
| `main.go` | The app's wiring: modules, migrations and the server |
| `config.go` | Settings from `[[.EnvPrefix]]_*` environment variables |
| `routes.go` | What is served where |
| `layout.go`, `pages.templ`, `static/` | The design and pages |
| `migrations/` | The app's database migrations |
| `Taskfile.yml` | The app's tasks; shared ones come from C4Stack |

## Configuration

| Variable | Required | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_PUBLIC_URL` | yes | The origin users reach the app on |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_DATABASE_URL` | yes | PostgreSQL URL; the only setting `migrate` reads |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_SECRET_KEY` | yes | At least 32 bytes, the same on every replica; signs CSRF tokens, seals cookies and keys sign-in's codes |
[[- if .Hanko]]
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_HANKO_API_URL` | yes | The Hanko tenant's API URL |
[[- else]]
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_EMAIL_FROM` | yes | The address sign-in codes and notices come from, on a domain with SPF, DKIM and DMARC |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_EMAIL_REPLY_TO` | no | Where replies go; notices ask people to reply, so a person must read them |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_SMTP_URL` | one of these | An SMTP server, `smtp://user:password@host:port`; it must offer STARTTLS off loopback |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_SCALEWAY_SECRET_KEY`, `[[.EnvPrefix]]_SCALEWAY_PROJECT_ID` | one of these | Scaleway Transactional Email, instead of SMTP |
[[- end]]
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_ADDR` | no | Listen address, `:8080` by default |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_TRUSTED_PROXIES` | behind a proxy | The proxies in front of the app, comma-separated addresses or CIDRs, whose forwarding headers give the client's address. Set exactly these: too few, and every client seems to come from the proxy and shares one limit on sign-in codes; too many, and clients choose the address they seem to come from. |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_LOG_LEVEL`, `[[.EnvPrefix]]_LOG_FORMAT` | no | `debug`…`error`; `json` (default) or `text` |

## Deploy

Give the app its settings as environment variables, with its secrets from a secret
store such as Infisical, never from a file in the image or the repository. Build and
push the image with `task container:push REGISTRY=…`. On each release:

1. Run the image with the `migrate` command as a one-off job. It needs only
   `[[.EnvPrefix]]_DATABASE_URL`.
2. Roll out the image with the `serve` command. Point readiness probes at
   `/health/ready` and liveness probes at `/health/live`.

[Operations]([[.Docs]]/operations.md) has the details and the runbooks.

## Upgrade C4Stack

```sh
task framework:update VERSION=vX.Y.Z
```

This moves the Go dependency and the shared tasks to the new release, then regenerates,
tests and builds. Read the release notes, then run `task db:migrate`.
